  "worked_solution": "First, let's solve for the missing values:\n\n- When $P\u2261\\text{T}$ and $Q\u2261\\text{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q\u2228\u00ac(P\u2228Q) & \u2261\\text{T}\u2228\u00ac(\\text{T}\u2228\\text{T}) \\\\  & \u2261\\text{T}\u2228\u00ac\\text{T} \\\\  & \u2261\\text{T}\u2228\\text{F} \\\\  & \u2261\\text{T}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- When $P\u2261\\text{T}$ and $Q\u2261\\text{F},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q\u2228\u00ac(P\u2228Q) & \u2261\\text{F}\u2228\u00ac(\\text{T}\u2228\\text{F}) \\\\  & \u2261\\text{F}\u2228\u00ac\\text{T} \\\\  & \u2261\\text{F}\u2228\\text{F} \\\\  & \u2261\\text{F}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- When $P\u2261\\text{F}$ and $Q\u2261\\text{F},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u00acP\u2228Q & \u2261\u00ac\\text{F}\u2228\\text{F} \\\\  & \u2261\\text{T}\u2228\\text{F} \\\\  & \u2261\\text{T}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOur completed table is shown below. \n\n| $\\,P\\,$ | $\\,Q\\,$ | $\\,Q\u2228\u00ac(P\u2228Q)\\,$ | $\\,\u00acP\u2228Q\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n\nTo determine whether $Q\u2228\u00ac(P\u2228Q)$ is logically equivalent to $\u00acP\u2228Q,$ we need to check whether their truth tables are equivalent.\n\nLooking at the last two columns, we see that they are the same $(\\text{T},\\text{F},\\text{T},\\text{T}).$ Therefore, we conclude that \n\n$$\nQ\u2228\u00ac(P\u2228Q)\u2261\u00acP\u2228Q.\n$$",
